---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    q: "How do I get my open-source AI project tracked on Radar?",
    a: `Open a submission using our <a href="/submit" class="link">Submit a Repo</a> template. Submissions are reviewed and imported within a few days. The radar also runs automated 4-layer discovery (topics, keywords, trending activity, and free-text search) daily to discover emerging repositories automatically.`
  },
  {
    q: "How often is the radar data refreshed?",
    a: `• <strong>Processing pipeline</strong>: Runs <strong>4 times daily</strong> (00:00, 06:00, 12:00, 18:00 UTC) to update stars, forks, issues, PRs, and re-compute Impact, Velocity, and Health scores.<br>
• <strong>Discovery pipeline</strong>: Runs <strong>twice daily</strong> (02:00, 14:00 UTC) to discover newly published or trending AI projects.<br>
• <strong>Website deployment</strong>: Automatically triggers after processing to publish the updated static dashboard to GitHub Pages.`
  },
  {
    q: "Why did my project's Velocity score drop even though star count increased?",
    a: `Radar uses <strong>three-axis scoring</strong>:
• <strong>Impact (40%)</strong>: Percentile ranking of stars, forks, and watchers.
• <strong>Velocity (35%)</strong>: 7-day and 30-day growth rate and acceleration, not absolute star volume.
• <strong>Health (25%)</strong>: Commit recency, release cadence, issue turnaround, and maintainer count.

If a project's star growth slows down relative to the prior week (e.g., from +100 stars/day to +20 stars/day), the acceleration drops, causing Velocity to decrease even while cumulative stars rise.`
  },
  {
    q: "How can I embed a dynamic badge on my GitHub README?",
    a: `Use the badge endpoint:
<pre><code>[![AI Radar Score](https://erbharatmalhotra.github.io/open-source-ai-radar/api/badges/OWNER__REPO/score.svg)](https://erbharatmalhotra.github.io/open-source-ai-radar/project/OWNER/REPO/)</code></pre>
Replace <code>OWNER__REPO</code> with your repository path separated by two underscores (e.g. <code>BerriAI__litellm</code>).`
  },
  {
    q: "Can I consume Radar data via API?",
    a: `Yes, all radar intelligence is published statically under <code>/api/</code>:
<ul>
<li>Top projects: <code>/api/top.json</code></li>
<li>All repos: <code>/api/repos.json</code> (and <code>/api/repos.csv</code>)</li>
<li>Category intelligence: <code>/api/categories.json</code></li>
<li>Anomaly alerts: <code>/api/anomalies.json</code></li>
<li>Breakout candidates: <code>/api/breakouts.json</code></li>
<li>Machine-readable dataset for LLMs: <code>/api/llms.txt</code></li>
</ul>
Full documentation is available at <a href="/api-docs" class="link">API Docs</a>.`
  },
  {
    q: "What do the score tiers mean?",
    a: `Scores are normalized 0–100 and bucketed into tiers:
<ul>
<li><strong>90–100</strong>: <span style="color:var(--purple)">Elite</span> — Category-defining projects</li>
<li><strong>75–89</strong>: <span style="color:var(--blue)">Leading</span> — Strong momentum & adoption</li>
<li><strong>60–74</strong>: <span style="color:var(--green)">Rising</span> — Healthy growth trajectory</li>
<li><strong>40–59</strong>: <span style="color:var(--amber)">Emerging</span> — Early traction</li>
<li><strong>0–39</strong>: <span style="color:var(--gray)">Discovering</span> — New or low activity</li>
</ul>`
  },
  {
    q: "How is the Health score calculated?",
    a: `Health (25% weight) combines:
<ul>
<li><strong>Commit recency</strong>: Days since last commit (lower = better)</li>
<li><strong>Release cadence</strong>: Frequency of tagged releases</li>
<li><strong>Issue turnaround</strong>: Median time to close issues</li>
<li><strong>Maintainer count</strong>: Number of distinct committers (more = resilient)</li>
</ul>
A project with frequent commits, regular releases, quick issue resolution, and multiple maintainers scores highest.`
  },
  {
    q: "Can I compare projects side-by-side?",
    a: `Yes! Use the <a href="/compare" class="link">Compare Tool</a> — enter up to 4 repositories to see Impact, Velocity, Health scores and historical trends side by side.`
  },
  {
    q: "What are Breakouts?",
    a: `Breakouts are projects with <strong>high Velocity + Health but lower Impact</strong> — they're accelerating fast but haven't hit mainstream visibility yet. The <a href="/breakouts" class="link">Breakouts page</a> surfaces these rising stars early.`
  },
  {
    q: "How do I report incorrect data?",
    a: `Open an issue on GitHub with the <strong>Data Correction</strong> template, or submit a fresh entry via <a href="/submit" class="link">Submit a Repo</a> — we'll re-process on the next pipeline run.`
  },
  {
    q: "Is the data open for research?",
    a: `Absolutely. All data is public via the <a href="/api-docs" class="link">API</a> (JSON/CSV). We also publish <code>/api/llms.txt</code> following the <a href="https://llmstxt.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="link">llms.txt convention</a> for AI agent consumption.`
  }
];
---

<Layout title="FAQ" description="Frequently asked questions about Open Source AI Radar.">
  <section class="hero-editorial" style="padding-bottom:var(--sp-8);">
    <h1><span class="accent">FAQ</span></h1>
    <p>Everything you need to know about how the radar works, scoring, badges, and API access.</p>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="card" style="padding:0; overflow:hidden;">
      <dl class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
          <div class="faq-item">
            <dt>
              <button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls={`faq-answer-${i}`}>
                <span>{faq.q}</span>
                <svg class="faq-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true"><polyline points="6 9 12 15 18 9"/></svg>
              </button>
            </dt>
            <dd id={`faq-answer-${i}`} class="faq-answer" hidden>
              <div class="faq-content" set:html={faq.a} />
            </dd>
          </div>
        ))}
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="card" style="padding:var(--sp-6); text-align:center;">
      <h2 style="font-size:var(--text-lg); margin-bottom:var(--sp-2);">Still have questions?</h2>
      <p style="color:var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom:var(--sp-4);">Open a discussion or submit an issue — we're happy to help.</p>
      <div style="display:flex; gap:var(--sp-3); justify-content:center; flex-wrap:wrap;">
        <a href="https://github.com/ErBharatMalhotra/open-source-ai-radar/discussions/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-primary">Start a Discussion</a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ErBharatMalhotra/open-source-ai-radar/issues/new/choose" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-secondary">Report an Issue</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .faq-list {
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .faq-item {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }
  .faq-question {
    width: 100%;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    padding: var(--sp-4) var(--sp-5);
    background: transparent;
    border: none;
    text-align: left;
    font: inherit;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--text);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background var(--transition-fast);
  }
  .faq-question:hover {
    background: var(--bg-elevated);
  }
  .faq-question:focus-visible {
    outline: 2px solid var(--accent);
    outline-offset: -2px;
  }
  .faq-icon {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    transition: transform var(--transition-fast);
  }
  .faq-question[aria-expanded="true"] .faq-icon {
    transform: rotate(180deg);
  }
  .faq-answer {
    padding: 0 var(--sp-5) var(--sp-5);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .faq-answer[hidden] {
    display: none;
  }
  .faq-content {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
  }
  .faq-content a.link {
    color: var(--accent);
    text-decoration: underline;
    text-underline-offset: 2px;
  }
  .faq-content a.link:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
  .faq-content code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.9em;
    background: var(--bg);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
  }
  .faq-content pre {
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0;
    padding: var(--sp-3);
    background: var(--bg);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    overflow-x: auto;
  }
  .faq-content pre code {
    background: transparent;
    padding: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
  }
  .faq-content ul {
    margin: var(--sp-3) 0;
    padding-left: var(--sp-6);
  }
  .faq-content li {
    margin: var(--sp-1) 0;
  }
  .faq-content strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .faq-question {
      padding: var(--sp-3) var(--sp-4);
      font-size: var(--text-sm);
    }
    .faq-answer {
      padding: 0 var(--sp-4) var(--sp-4);
    }
  }
</style>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-question').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const expanded = btn.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
      const answer = document.getElementById(btn.getAttribute('aria-controls'));
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
      if (!expanded) {
        answer.hidden = false;
      } else {
        answer.hidden = true;
      }
    });
  });
</script>